ola: Heads-up: PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/556 needs small runnable SDK examples for the errors doc (429s, timeouts, context-limit fallbacks). Reviewers want copy-pasteable snippets for JS + Python and a one-line infra note.
chen: Happy to add. Suggested defaults: 3 attempts total, initial backoff 400ms, cap 1800ms, simple jitter. Also show a cached-response fallback and a compact-model fallback.
marta: For JS please use AbortController for timeouts and show explicit Authorization header reminder. For Python use requests.Session and show raising on 429.
ola: Draft JS (short):
```js
// fetch + AbortController + retry with jitter
async function call(url, opts = {}) {
  const max = 2; let i=0;
  while (true) {
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const t = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), opts.timeout || 5000);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { signal: ctrl.signal, headers: { 'Content-Type':'application/json', 'Authorization':'Bearer <REDACTED>' } });
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (res.status === 429) throw new Error('RATE_LIMIT');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (e) {
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (e.name === 'AbortError') throw new Error('TIMEOUT');
      if (i++ >= max) throw e;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.min(1800, 400 * 2 ** i) + Math.random()*200));
    }
  }
}
```
chen: Python snippet (compact):
```py
# requests + simple retry + cached fallback
import time, requests
s = requests.Session()

def call(url, payload, retries=2):
    for i in range(retries+1):
        r = s.post(url, json=payload, timeout=5)
        if r.status_code == 429:
            raise Exception('RATE_LIMIT')
        r.raise_for_status()
        return r.json()
    time.sleep(0.5*(2**i))

def gen_with_fallback(primary, compact, payload, cache):
    try:
        return call(primary, payload)
    except Exception:
        if cache.get('last'):
            return cache['last']
        return call(compact, payload)
```
marta: Nice and concise. Add infra note: "Set client timeout to be slightly less than backend processing timeout so clients can retry/cleanup (e.g., client=5s, backend=6s)." Also add a doc cross-link to context-limits and fallback-policies.
